How to delimit pages in the .Lot file.

The ../Text/$1.txt file is a sequence of all the lines in the form.
The lines from all pages of the form are listed in order.
The exception is when subsequent pages are carbon copies of page 1.
In that case only the first page is sequenced.

Your ../PreLot/$1.pre file presents the lines as being on one page.
You now have to separate the pages.

If the form is a single page then that page is delimited with:
PgS at the start and EndPgS at the end.

If the form is two pages then:
The first page is delimited with
PgF at the start and EndPgF at the end.
The second page is delimited with
PgL at the start and EndPgL at the end.

If the form is three or more pages
The first page is delimited with
PgF at the start and EndPgF at the end.
Subsequent pages are delimited with
PgM at the start and EndPgM at the end.
The last page is delimited with
PgL at the start and EndPgL at the end.

If the subsequent pages are carbon copies of the first
copy the lines of the first page as often as necessary
to create the subsequent pages.
Then delimit the pages as directed above.
You may have to make slight changes to some pages if
they are not exact duplicates.